WEBVTT

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.350
Get in.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.750
Hurry up!

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.260
I can see it.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.380
How creepy can a place look?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.240
Hey, Joe!

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.640
Wake up! I can see the prison!

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.980
Hey, Joe.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.310
Stop exaggerating...

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.470
Let me see...

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.230
A nice little castle.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:23.890
You're scared

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.580
just 'cause we're behind enemy lines?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.130
Looks like you picked the wrong team.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.260
By the way,

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.620
why is it so quiet?

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.570
I can't believe they're holding hundreds of people here.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.480
I've got a bad feeling...

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.820
Why is it so quiet?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.630
Someone's here.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:48.490
They're here.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.690
A new customer.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.380
I'm transferring Yabuki Joe and Nishi Kanichi.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.590
They are in your custody now.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.590
Please confirm their identities.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.090
Good work.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.090
Barred windows wherever you look...

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.140
Nice security around here.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.890
You, the small one.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.560
Yeah, what can I do for you?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.210
They call you "Yabuki," right?

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.320
I'll be watching every step you take.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.900
Don't get any ideas.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.400
Ideas?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.450
Dreams of the outside...

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.410
Ideas of escaping...

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.810
W-We would never think of it.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.960
Let me tell you about Nogiku Island.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.590
You guys are here.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.050
The west coast, north coast, east coast,

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.300
and south coast are all sheer cliffs.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:37.700
They are surrounded by sharp rocks, so you'll crack your skull if you jump.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.900
Th-There's no way we would try to escape.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.920
I was talking to the small one!

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:49.960
Even if you manage to escape the prison, there's only one ship every ten days,

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.220
we carefully check it,

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.360
and there are no other boats.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.290
This is the end of the line.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.110
Sounds interesting.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:06.880
I'm the kind of guy who likes a challenge.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.760
Joe, what are you saying!?

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.920
Just kidding.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:15.810
I see...

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.440
Enough.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.220
Whatever you like...

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:23.490
Just remember that merely discussing a plan will lengthen your sentence.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.830
Don't get any stupid ideas.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.450
Y-Yes, sir. Understood.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.020
There are a total of 300 prisoners.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:46.800
They are divided into groups of twenty, living in buildings one through fifteen.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.720
You will be in cell block six.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.390
Warden, sir, I have a favor to ask!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.190
What are you doing, yelling like that?

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.180
Quiet down for God's sake.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:02.570
I'll...

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:05.400
I'll be a model prisoner.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.330
I'll reform. Just do one thing for me...

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.000
It's the middle of the night, be quiet.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.710
Hurry up and ask.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.280
What do you want?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:19.370
P-Please don't let the other prisoners gang up on us.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.250
P-Please keep an eye on us!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.750
Wh-What?

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.210
You look ridiculous, Nishi.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.660
That's what you used to do in the holding cell...

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.790
It'll be your turn soon.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.700
Be prepared.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.450
That was nothing.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:52.170
If the hardened criminals here get us...

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:05.360
That kind of thing is forbidden here, don't worry.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.230
Hurry up and get in.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.660
That's an amazing door.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:21.020
It's the kind you'd expect to find a pirate's treasure behind.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.330
Okay, get in.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.520
Everyone's asleep.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:29.410
We'll leave the introductions for tomorrow.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.030
Go to sleep and keep quiet, understand?

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.520
Warden!

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.830
Stay a while... Relax...

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.300
Wh-What are you saying?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.490
Get in, get in, get in!

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.640
Your futons are over there.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.000
Get ready and go to bed.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.540
Warden!

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.290
Wait! Wait...

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.340
Wait! Wait...

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.610
Joe...

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:05.560
What will we do... if... if they wake up?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.910
Stop being stupid. Why are you shaking?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.400
They're waking up!

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.090
That won't do anything...

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:18.420
Do you think they'll go easy on you if you look scared?

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.560
All right, Nishi,

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.810
we had a long trip from Tokyo.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:22.370
I'm tired,

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.600
let's get some sleep.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.970
Try not to step on their feet...

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.300
What?

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.130
Crap!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.220
Sorry 'bout that, Senpai...

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:34.140
Did it hurt?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.130
All right, then.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.640
I got one for you too.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.100
Sleep already.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.100
<i>Quiet...</i>

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.140
Be quiet when you unroll the futon.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:47.780
Shut up, I've got it...

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.160
By the way, something smells.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.240
It's the bathroom.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:56.150
How come we get the worst spot? This is gross, damn it!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.610
Please, Joe, don't upset anyone. Just go to sleep.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:03.610
Well,

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:07.520
the new guys always get the worst spot. It's expected.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:09.120
Let's just pinch our noses.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.670
I'll get some sleep.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:18.100
I-I'm extremely sorry for my friend's insolence.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.470
Good night.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:21.430
Sleep well.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.780
There's no doubt. We really are a long way from home.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.910
I told you they'd wake up!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.320
Calm down,

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.010
they've been awake the whole time.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.170
Isn't that right?

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:14.030
You're pretty brave to talk to us like that.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.180
S-Senpai... I'll be joining you starting today.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:21.580
My name is Nishi... Nishi Kanichi. I'm not worth your time.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.300
I look forward to staying with you.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.990
What about you, runt?

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:29.920
It's my turn?

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:36.500
Sorry to make you wait... Let me tell you who I am!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.510
I-Idiot... You're stupid, Joe!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:42.630
I was born without seeing a mother's smile or knowing my father's name.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.550
I've spent the last fifteen years getting into trouble.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.080
I didn't fit in at the orphanage.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:51.720
I seek a free world.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:57.300
I've escaped more than ten times.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.230
My punch has been strong since I was a child.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.740
No one would dispute that.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.530
For a long time, while I was in the slums,

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.700
a strange old guy stalked me.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:11.540
Enlightened with inspiration, I took a once in a lifetime bet with a small gang.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.040
I managed to swindle a million ryo through the mass media.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.040
[Note: A "ryo" is a gold coin which used to be the Japanese currency.]

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:21.850
I even evaded the police, until that old man caught me and beat me up.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:24.430
Then, I was sent to a holding cell.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.100
Now,

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.810
I held my own in the holding cell.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.730
This guy is a leftover from it.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.960
Justice has finally taken me to Nogiku Island's

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.990
Toko High Security Juvenile Prison.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:49.680
I'm Yabuki Joe, the renegade!

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.630
Well,

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:51.840
that's about it for me...

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.000
Did you get all that, guys?

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.000
You idiot...

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.500
You asshole! You jerk! I don't even know you.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.850
So, it's five against one...

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:04.010
Good enough for me.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.200
Well,

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.270
it's time for you two to get some sleep.

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.760
Looks like it...

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.280
Some sleep?

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:25.720
Rest in peace.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:32.950
Rest in peace.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.340
Turn the light off for them.

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.970
They said it's too bright to sleep.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.250
All right, it's off.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.420
Sweet dreams...

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:24.490
Th-That's not fair!

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.560
Such cowards!

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:28.440
No fair!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:29.550
Someone save me!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.260
They're out cold.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.610
That was too easy.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.120
Rest in peace.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:56.080
However,

00:14:56.080 --> 00:15:00.090
that's just the beginning of our little introduction.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:04.240
This isn't some temporary situation like the holding cell.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.310
Anyone in here has a minimum sentence of thirteen months.

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.590
We'll have to get to know each other...

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.230
We have plenty of time to become friends.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.740
Hey! Joe! Hang in there!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.180
Get up!

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.170
Joe, get up!

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.830
Joe!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.200
Keep going!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.760
Get up, Joe!

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.350
Joe!

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:54.850
It was a dream?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:58.260
I wonder if he's doing all right...{TLC}

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.580
Now, then...

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:00.710
Time to go.

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:15.980
Sachi, is that you?

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:17.740
What in the world are you doing?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.240
Nothing!

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.220
I get it.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.720
What?

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:26.960
You ran away from home.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.260
You peed on the futon, right?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.680
I don't do that anymore!

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:34.260
I hate you, old man!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.220
Then...?

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.830
I had a dream.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:39.260
A dream?

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.960
I've been having the same dream over and over.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.240
I thought I'd have it again if I fell asleep.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:47.810
So you came here?

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:52.830
I don't want to see Joe get beaten to death...

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.910
What? You too?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.410
You're having the same dream?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.150
I wonder...

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.410
Sachi, don't worry about it.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:11.380
Long ago, people would call it an "inverse dream" -
 what's happening is the opposite of what you see.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:17.930
Two people having a dream like that means something good is going to happen to Joe.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.640
In that case, the dream really isn't scary at all.

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:27.950
That's right, so why not get some sleep?

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.220
Okay, no problem.

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.630
Thanks, see you later.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.270
No more wetting the bed! Drip, drip, drip...

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:40.870
You worry me even in my dreams...

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:44.550
Joe, you're such a pain.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:05.770
[Note: This schedule lists the daily routine of the prisoners.]

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.460
Damn, it's loud.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.780
Damn it.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.160
I'm awake!

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.290
Look over there! He's gone!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.300
What!?

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.220
What?

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.510
That bastard.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.820
Didn't we beat the crap out of them yesterday?

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.310
Is he eating breakfast?

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.880
This one is still here.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.320
He ran away.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:40.260
That's not possible, is it?

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.740
You! Get up!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.210
Ouch!

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.220
Shut up!

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:46.480
Hey!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.290
Where is the little one?

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.940
The little one?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.490
Tell us where that guy went!

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.780
Don't say he just disappeared.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.840
Don't ask stupid questions.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:01.690
That's not possible... People don't just disappear like ghosts!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.420
L-Look at that!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:14.820
He's sleeping in the best spot, with ten futons!

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:18.760
Hey, runt, where are the guys who were using those?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:22.260
Them? They're in there.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.170
The toilet.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.400
Wh-What the hell?

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:40.110
I got beaten so badly that I couldn't sleep by the toilet.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.990
I asked them to switch, but they wouldn't,

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.660
so I gave them a little pat on the head and threw them in there.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.560
You bastard...

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.830
The new guy should know his place.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:55.140
You are an unbeatable star.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:56.350
I won't complain anymore,

00:19:56.350 --> 00:20:01.340
I'll just wait and see what you do in here.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.230
Get him.

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:08.310
What are you guys doing here, Block Six?

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.860
You should have cleaned and be lining up for breakfast.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:13.130
You won't get any breakfast if you don't hurry.

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:14.920
Hurry it up.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:17.520
Yes, sir.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.140
I was gonna beat you to death.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.820
You're in luck, runt.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.320
Anyway, put away those futons.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.040
I don't need you to tell me to put away my own futon.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:34.790
Don't just stare at me. Go clean up your own stuff already!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.350
It's common knowledge that that's the new guy's job.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:42.340
Too bad, I'm not your slave.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:43.060
What!?

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.100
What are you saying?

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:45.100
You idiot.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.290
We won't put up with this.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.850
Excuse me.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.350
I'll take care of it for him.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.540
We weren't talking to you!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.770
I told the runt fry to do it.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.230
Everyone, shut up!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.050
I'm getting tired of all this "new guy" talk.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.270
It's starting to piss me off.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.750
Joe, stop it.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.320
Ready?

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.340
Come from all directions...

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:11.950
Hey!

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.070
Hey!

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:14.160
Warden!

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.460
Please come in here!

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:18.270
There's a problem!

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:20.010
Come quickly!

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:21.170
What?

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.140
What is this?

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:25.880
Um... Um...

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:31.140
They're trying to make us do everything just because we're new.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.640
What?

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:38.650
Are we supposed to do everything just because we're new?

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.980
There's no rule like that.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:43.650
Look, they're all doing it.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.160
Why are you wasting my time?

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:59.670
Nishi, you did it.

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:02.590
They sure do talk big,

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.330
but look what happens when a guard comes.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:23.600
The runt is taking things too far, but not for long...

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.460
We'll get him later.

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:28.140
Too bad for him, he took it a bit too far.

00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:36.430
Rest in peace.

00:22:33.800 --> 00:22:37.110
<i>Don't worry, Nishi, we're getting out of here.</i>

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:39.100
I can't bear another day in this place.

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:41.080
I'll figure something out.

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:47.090
There's no way I can stop you, so I guess I'll help however I can.

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:50.290
What are you saying? We're a team.

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:52.670
Look at me. I'm a coward, and I'm weak.

00:22:52.670 --> 00:22:54.510
You at least have to get yourself out.

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:04.440
Who is that?

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.450
He's staring right at us with those crazy eyes.

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:11.360
He's certainly got my attention.

00:23:30.230 --> 00:23:36.000
Joe meets a man with an iron body and a burning will.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.770
His name is Rikiishi Toru.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:41.520
He was a pro boxer but is now in prison.

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:47.410
He is getting in the way of Joe's plan to break out.

00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:48.790
So,

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.570
now that he's met his archrival,

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:53.740
which way is tomorrow!?
